      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please stop thinking about sealing it up with glue; that is a dangerous idea for a puncture wound and can trap bacteria deep inside. Instead, keep the wound covered with a sterile, clean dressing and keep the area elevated above your heart. For immediate antiseptic action, use an over-the-counter iodine solution, but a proper medical evaluation for tetanus and deep cleaning is non-negotiable. You must prioritize getting checked out by a healthcare professional as soon as possible.",
