      "content": "Do not pour peroxide or alcohol directly into a deep puncture wound; these harsh chemicals can damage the tissue and actually delay healing. The best way to irrigate the wound is by gently flushing it with copious amounts of clean, running tap water or sterile saline solution. If you absolutely cannot get to a doctor, keep the wound covered and monitor it closely for signs of infection like increasing redness or pus. Remember, while cleaning is important, professional medical care is what truly prevents severe complications.",
